        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಕೊರಗು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕೊರಗು — koragu — \"to pine; to brood\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕೆಲಸ ಹೋದ ಮೇಲೆ ಅವನು ದಿನವೂ ಕೊರಗುತ್ತಿದ್ದನು. kelasa hōda mēle avanu dinavū koraguttiddanu. After he lost his job, he used to brood every day."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಕೊರಗಿದೆ, koragide."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A quiet, long sorrow kept inside: ಮನಸ್ಸಿನಲ್ಲೇ ಕೊರಗು (koragu), to grieve in silence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕೊರಗು (koragu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 1778 gives Kannada koragu, \"to lose its sap, shrivel, waste away\", and also \"to sorrow\". A grief that dries a person up is the picture behind it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
