          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮರುಗು — marugu — \"to feel pity; to grieve for\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಗಾಯಗೊಂಡ ಹಕ್ಕಿಯನ್ನು ನೋಡಿ ಮಗು ಮರುಗಿತು. gāyagoṇḍa hakkiyannu nōḍi magu marugitu. Seeing the injured bird, the child felt sorry for it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಮರುಗಿದೆ, marugide."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The one you feel for takes -ಗಾಗಿ: ಅವನಿಗಾಗಿ ಮರುಗು (marugu), to feel for him."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮರುಗು (marugu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 4769 lists Kannada maṟugu, \"to burn, be very hot\", and from there \"to suffer, be distressed, grieve\". Pity is pictured as a burning inside."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
