          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸಂಕಟ — saṅkaṭa — \"anguish; distress\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅಜ್ಜಿಯ ಕಾಯಿಲೆ ನೋಡಿ ನನಗೆ ಸಂಕಟ ಆಯಿತು. ajjiya kāyile nōḍi nanage saṅkaṭa āyitu. Seeing grandmother's illness, I felt anguish."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A tight, pressing pain of the mind, and also a tight spot: ಸಂಕಟದಲ್ಲಿ ಸಿಕ್ಕಿಕೊ, to be caught in a crisis."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸಂಕಟ (saṅkaṭa) is borrowed from Sanskrit saṃkaṭa, \"brought together, narrow, crowded; dangerous, critical\" (Monier-Williams). Kannada uses it for a narrow place of the mind: distress."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
