              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪಶ್ಚಾತ್ತಾಪ — paścāttāpa — \"remorse; repentance\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸುಳ್ಳು ಹೇಳಿದ್ದಕ್ಕೆ ಅವನಿಗೆ ಪಶ್ಚಾತ್ತಾಪ ಆಯಿತು. suḷḷu hēḷiddakke avanige paścāttāpa āyitu. He felt remorse for having lied."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "For what: -ಕ್ಕೆ. ಪಶ್ಚಾತ್ತಾಪ (paścāttāpa) ಪಡು, to repent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪಶ್ಚಾತ್ತಾಪ (paścāttāpa) is borrowed from Sanskrit paścāttāpa, literally \"after-pain\": sorrow, regret, repentance (Monier-Williams). It is built from paścāt, \"afterwards\", and tāpa, \"heat, pain\"."
            }
          ]
        },
